    "narrative": "For today\u2019s slate, **Gunnar Henderson** stands as our premier offensive anchor with a commanding score of 81.877, bolstered by a 10% boost for hitting out of the leadoff spot and a favorable 14% platoon advantage against Singer. Following closely in utility, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.662) and **Kyle Tucker** (71.617) provide high-floor production, with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefiting from a soft matchup against Keller, whose 4.60 xERA allows for maximum damage on the basepaths\u2014a critical factor given our emphasis on SB scarcity. **Heliot Ramos** also earns a strong recommendation (69.026) due to a park-adjusted 14% lift and a 19% SP skill advantage against Feltner, confirming him as a core part of our mid-order production.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Nolan Schanuel** on the bench. Despite a solid 50.859 rating, he narrowly missed the starting cut because our current outfield and utility configurations offer more aggressive SB-upside and higher raw efficiency against today\u2019s specific starter profiles. While **Miguel Vargas** flashed an elite 0.403 xwOBA, his score of 44.409 remains suppressed by the tough matchup against Williams, leaving him as a high-leverage depth piece rather than a primary starter. We are monitoring **Liam Hicks** (48.276) closely; his matchup against Perkins is the risk point of the day, as a 16% negative SP skill adjustment drags down an otherwise solid base projection. Managers should ensure all lineup-pending statuses are updated, as any shift in order for **Sam Antonacci** or **Brayan Rocchio** could necessitate a pivot if their projected 10% and 15% efficiency boosts vanish due to defensive repositioning.",
